      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "docs/cookbook/autoregressive/GLM/GLM-5.3-Flash.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ import { benchmarks } from \"/src/snippets/configs/zai-org/glm-5.3-flash-benchmar\n <Deployment config={config} benchmarks={benchmarks} />\n \n <Note>\n-Generated commands leave `--mamba-full-memory-ratio` at its `0.9` default, which is a generic starting point rather than a workload-tuned split: too low starves the KDA state pool and clamps `max_running_requests`, too high over-provisions it and shrinks the KV pool. Use the repo-local [`compute-mamba-ratio`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.claude/skills/compute-mamba-ratio/SKILL.md) skill to compute the balanced ratio — or the `--max-mamba-cache-size` pin to use instead — from your average request length and the two pool sizes printed in one boot log. See [Size both memory pools](#size-both-memory-pools) for what each pool caps.\n+Generated commands leave `--mamba-full-memory-ratio` at its `0.9` default, which is a generic starting point rather than a workload-tuned split: too low starves the KDA state pool and clamps `max_running_requests`, too high over-provisions it and shrinks the KV pool. Use the repo-local [`compute-mamba-ratio`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/compute-mamba-ratio/SKILL.md) skill to compute the balanced ratio — or the `--max-mamba-cache-size` pin to use instead — from your average request length and the two pool sizes printed in one boot log. See [Size both memory pools](#size-both-memory-pools) for what each pool caps.\n </Note>\n \n ## Playground",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/f66735a2fbb17ac64296d7bec15494516c8de9b2/docs%2Fcookbook%2Fautoregressive%2FGLM%2FGLM-5.3-Flash.mdx",
